@startuml flip_prediction
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #34495E
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor #15263F
  BorderColor #2E6DA4
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FBF6E7
skinparam noteBorderColor #D9B85B

title RQ3 — Does pre-measured disagreement D(x) predict KV-compression flips?\n(leakage-safe pipeline; ILLUSTRATIVE 5-fold CV AUROC)

rectangle "**Full-cache** forward pass" as FC #EAF1FB
rectangle "Localization signals\n(within one substrate)" as SIG #EAF1FB
rectangle "**D(x)** = 1 - mean pairwise Spearman" as DX #D6F5DE

rectangle "**Compressed** pass\nH2O / SnapKV @ budget" as CC #FDEBD0
rectangle "Correctness (F1>=0.5 / EM)\nflip = correct -> wrong" as FL #FDEBD0

rectangle "Logistic: flip ~ D(x) + confounds\n(length, gold-depth, answer-entropy)\n5-fold CV · LRT · calibration" as MODEL #FCF3CF

FC --> SIG
SIG --> DX
CC --> FL
DX --> MODEL
FL --> MODEL

note bottom of CC
  **Leakage rule (§9.3 / gate 11.3c).** D(x) is computed from the
  full-cache pass **only**; the compressed run can never influence
  the feature that predicts its own outcome. Enforced by the type
  system (DisagreementScore refuses to exist otherwise).
end note

legend bottom
==  5-fold CV AUROC — does D(x) beat the difficulty proxies?  (illustrative)  ==
|= model |= AUROC |=  |
|= confound-only (length, depth, entropy) | 0.61 | <color:#fdae61>**#############**</color><color:#D9D9D9>#######</color> |
|= D(x) only                              | 0.68 | <color:#a6d96a>**###############**</color><color:#D9D9D9>#####</color> |
|= **D(x) + confounds (full)**            | **0.74** | <color:#1a9850>**#################**</color><color:#D9D9D9>###</color> |
incremental AUROC (D(x) over confounds) = **+0.13**   ·   likelihood-ratio test chi2(1), p < 0.01
endlegend

@enduml
